%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
.md
# Integration of Plotly Library
An API of the plotly.js library is available from the Wolfram Kernel. There is a 1:1 correspondence between JavaScript numbers, arrays, and objects. Please see [their API](https://plotly.com/javascript/) for all features.

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: markdown
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
# Integration of Plotly Library
An API of the plotly.js library is available from the Wolfram Kernel. There is a 1:1 correspondence between JavaScript numbers, arrays, and objects. Please see [their API](https://plotly.com/javascript/) for all features.

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Props:
  Hidden: true
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
.md
## Basic Charts
When you call `Plotly`, it acts as a constructor to a corresponding object.

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: markdown
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
## Basic Charts
When you call `Plotly`, it acts as a constructor to a corresponding object.

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
plot = Plotly[<|
  "y"->RandomReal[{-1,1}, 10],
  "mode"->"lines"
|>]

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
(*VB[*)(PlotlyInstance[FrontEndRef["F2dfcb8b1-0f3d-47ea-8ea2-c766ee623288"],WindowObj[<|"Socket" -> USocketObject[6]|>]])(*,*)(*"1:eJxTTMoPSmNkYGAoZgESHvk5KRCeEJBwK8rPK3HNS3GtSE0uLUlMykkNVgUJG6WkJSdZJBnqGqQZp+iamKcm6lqkJhrpJpubmaWmmhkZG1lYAACruBZR"*)(*]VB*)

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Props:
  Hidden: true
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
.md
To add more traces to an existing plot dynamically, call a dedicated method.

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: markdown
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
To add more traces to an existing plot dynamically, call a dedicated method.

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Props:
  Hidden: false
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
PlotlyAddTraces[plot, {<|"y"->RandomReal[{-1,1}, 10]|>}]

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Props:
  Hidden: true
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
.md
Using the Plotly API, one can also extend plots and animate them. Please see more examples [here](https://jerryi.github.io/wljs-docs/frontend/Reference/Plotly/PlotlyExtendTraces).

To plot multiple traces from the beginning, supply arrays for the `x` and `y` axes.

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: markdown
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Using the Plotly API, one can also extend plots and animate them. Please see more examples [here](https://jerryi.github.io/wljs-docs/frontend/Reference/Plotly/PlotlyExtendTraces).

To plot multiple traces from the beginning, supply arrays for the `x` and `y` axes.

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
trace := <|
	"y" -> RandomReal[{-1,1}, 10], 
	"type" -> "line" 
|>;

Plotly[{trace, trace, trace}]

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
(*VB[*)(PlotlyInstance[FrontEndRef["F294cd838-47ca-44c7-b0ff-6e0e71762006"],WindowObj[<|"Socket" -> USocketObject[6]|>]])(*,*)(*"1:eJxTTMoPSmNkYGAoZgESHvk5KRCeEJBwK8rPK3HNS3GtSE0uLUlMykkNVgUJG1maJKdYGFvompgnJ+qamCSb6yYZpKXpmqUapJobmpsZGRiYAQCYTRWP"*)(*]VB*)

